{"idea_id_local": "I-001-001", "cluster_id": "I-001-S1", "cycle_id": "cycle-001", "subagent_id": "B-001", "persona": "dreamer", "seed": "s1", "idea_title": "Self-rewriting LOOP.md as ship target", "idea_text": "The meta-loop's ship target IS its own LOOP.md, rewritten every cycle as the γ-synthesis output. Each cycle produces a new hash-versioned protocol; the prior protocol is archived, never edited in place. The loop ships by mutating its own protocol, not by producing an external artifact.", "warrant": "Existing loops already version LOOP.md via git commits; promoting it to ship target makes explicit what was implicit.", "warrant_hash": "sha256:1c44757b8612bf5b15caa4ccd137df18", "verdict": "INCONCLUSIVE", "confidence": 0.62, "status": "advance", "updated_at": "2026-07-24T23:34:08.124626+00:00"}
{"idea_id_local": "I-001-002", "cluster_id": "I-001-S1", "cycle_id": "cycle-001", "subagent_id": "B-001", "persona": "dreamer", "seed": "s1", "idea_title": "Wave-zero \"domain probe\" for autonomy-criteria discovery", "idea_text": "A mandatory reconnaissance wave (Wave Ω) runs before protocol authoring: the agent dispatches N cheap probes into the target domain (read its artifacts, run a no-op action, observe which signals return without HITL) and derives the domain's autonomy criteria from what came back. Discovered criteria become inputs to the LOOP.md being authored.", "warrant": "cd-review already discovers its scope from the codebase via §4 slicing; this generalizes that discovery to the autonomy dimension.", "warrant_hash": "sha256:b5a352c11eda3d68c90000d0417712e0", "verdict": "INCONCLUSIVE", "confidence": 0.62, "status": "advance", "updated_at": "2026-07-24T23:34:08.124626+00:00"}
{"idea_id_local": "I-001-003", "cluster_id": "I-001-S3", "cycle_id": "cycle-001", "subagent_id": "B-001", "persona": "dreamer", "seed": "s1", "idea_title": "Typed \"ports\" as composition primitive", "idea_text": "Every authored LOOP.md declares typed input ports (what cycle-scope inputs it consumes) and typed output ports (what artifacts it produces). Composition = port-matching. `loop-forge + brainstorm` works because brainstorm emits an `ideas-port` and loop-forge consumes a `problem-port`.", "warrant": "brainstorm and cd-review already implicitly produce known artifact types (idea-docs, audit-fix pairs); ports make that explicit.", "warrant_hash": "sha256:0ed9b52631eff83a524e5d78a07d0a44", "verdict": "ADVANCE", "confidence": 0.72, "status": "advance", "updated_at": "2026-07-24T23:34:08.124626+00:00"}
{"idea_id_local": "I-001-004", "cluster_id": "I-001-S2", "cycle_id": "cycle-001", "subagent_id": "B-001", "persona": "dreamer", "seed": "s1", "idea_title": "\"Loop-itch\" detector for mid-task extraction", "idea_text": "Any subagent, at any wave, may file a `loop-itch.md` when it detects the sub-problem it's grinding on exhibits autonomy-envelope properties (repeating decision points, multiple wave-worthy slices, would benefit from its own stop conditions). Orchestrator promotes top-itched sub-problems to a mid-cycle extraction step that spawns a child loop-forge cycle.", "warrant": "brainstorm already uses persona×seed diversification to detect when an idea warrants its own research dossier; itch-filing generalizes that detection.", "warrant_hash": "sha256:1920fdb20c1f586e88c4964a685aed39", "verdict": "ADVANCE", "confidence": 0.75, "status": "advance", "updated_at": "2026-07-24T23:34:08.124626+00:00"}
{"idea_id_local": "I-001-005", "cluster_id": "I-001-S4", "cycle_id": "cycle-001", "subagent_id": "B-001", "persona": "dreamer", "seed": "s1", "idea_title": "Self-simulation gate before ship", "idea_text": "Before shipping a candidate LOOP.md, the meta-loop runs ONE synthetic cycle of that LOOP.md on a fabricated input (e.g., \"author a loop for sorting numbers\") and ships only if the simulation closes cleanly — no `fatal_blocked`, no unresolved `Stopped at`. The sim is the verify step; the protocol must run itself before it ships.", "warrant": "cd-review already runs Wave D pre-PR review on its own work; self-simulation is the structural analog applied to protocols.", "warrant_hash": "sha256:0f8192fd2d307b530021bc2a166f0fe2", "verdict": "ADVANCE", "confidence": 0.5, "status": "advance", "updated_at": "2026-07-24T23:34:08.124626+00:00"}
{"idea_id_local": "I-001-006", "cluster_id": "I-001-S1", "cycle_id": "cycle-001", "subagent_id": "B-001", "persona": "dreamer", "seed": "s1", "idea_title": "Autonomy-as-contract wave (PO reversal)", "idea_text": "PO: instead of the agent deciding what autonomy means, the target domain declares its own autonomy budget. A Wave-Ω' presents the domain with a draft autonomy envelope; the domain (via its existing artifacts, a stub, or a representative oracle) accepts or rejects clauses; the loop ships only when both sign. Autonomy is negotiated, not authored.", "warrant": "Brainstorm's launcher↔cycle-scope split already treats autonomy as a negotiated boundary (launcher sets scope, worker sets execution); this surfaces that negotiation as a first-class wave.", "warrant_hash": "sha256:81139afd73ce322759fe423260ec96c2", "verdict": "INCONCLUSIVE", "confidence": 0.62, "status": "advance", "updated_at": "2026-07-24T23:34:08.124626+00:00"}
{"idea_id_local": "I-001-007", "cluster_id": "I-001-S5", "cycle_id": "cycle-001", "subagent_id": "B-001", "persona": "dreamer", "seed": "s1", "idea_title": "Loop genome with lineage + mutation operator", "idea_text": "Every authored LOOP.md carries a `lineage` block: parent loop hashes, mutation operator (e.g., `+wave`, `port-swap`, `compose`, `reduce`), and inheritance mask. cd-review and brainstorm are designated founder genomes. Combinability is a property of compatible lineages, not ad-hoc.", "warrant": "brainstorm already uses novelty-archive hashing for idea dedup; genome hashing is the protocol-level analog.", "warrant_hash": "sha256:04a557375fa8fcc2ffee2cb394d3666b", "verdict": "ADVANCE", "confidence": 0.78, "status": "advance", "updated_at": "2026-07-24T23:34:08.124626+00:00"}
{"idea_id_local": "I-001-PORTFOLIO", "cluster_id": "I-001-S5", "cycle_id": "cycle-001", "subagent_id": "B-002", "persona": "dreamer", "seed": "s2", "idea_title": "PORTFOLIO.md as cross-loop single source of truth", "idea_text": "A top-level `PORTFOLIO.md` catalogs every authored loop with its autonomy envelope, combinability graph, and version, rewritten each meta-cycle. LOOP.md stays local truth; PORTFOLIO.md is the inter-loop truth.", "warrant": "Combinability needs an addressable registry; without it, combinations are re-derived every cycle.", "warrant_hash": "sha256:9d51cda5c43818da905ff3cea91e8ade", "verdict": "ADVANCE", "confidence": 0.78, "status": "advance", "updated_at": "2026-07-24T23:34:08.124626+00:00"}
{"idea_id_local": "I-002-LOOPSCOPE", "cluster_id": null, "cycle_id": "cycle-001", "subagent_id": "B-002", "persona": "dreamer", "seed": "s2", "idea_title": "Two-layer harness at the loop-authoring scale", "idea_text": "Loop-forge launcher spawns a loop-scope agent owning ONE loop end-to-end (skeleton → stress-test → ship LOOP.md). Launcher polls `loop-status.json` + `LOOP-DRAFT.md` \"Stopped at\". Peer process, never a child. Runs waves of in-process subagents.", "warrant": "The harness survives context exhaustion; mid-loop checkpointing (I-004) extends it.", "warrant_hash": "sha256:20b645d118fe01a32c3fcfac1f80e0cd", "verdict": null, "confidence": null, "status": "deferred", "updated_at": "2026-07-24T23:34:08.124626+00:00"}
{"idea_id_local": "I-003-COMPOSE", "cluster_id": "I-001-S3", "cycle_id": "cycle-001", "subagent_id": "B-002", "persona": "dreamer", "seed": "s2", "idea_title": "3-state combinability verdicts between loops", "idea_text": "Each new loop is combinability-tested against each existing loop. Each pair issues: COMPOSE (safe to chain), CONFLICT (autonomy envelopes collide — both claim same `runs/`), ORTHOGONAL (co-exist, no chaining). CONFLICT forces rename or refuse-to-ship.", "warrant": "Loops declare resource surfaces in a machine-readable block; verdict = graph-coloring check.", "warrant_hash": "sha256:d7b661051aa0bede3d8650931491df54", "verdict": "ADVANCE", "confidence": 0.72, "status": "advance", "updated_at": "2026-07-24T23:34:08.124626+00:00"}
{"idea_id_local": "I-004-EXTRACT", "cluster_id": "I-001-S2", "cycle_id": "cycle-001", "subagent_id": "B-002", "persona": "dreamer", "seed": "s2", "idea_title": "Mid-loop extraction checkpoint", "idea_text": "When the loop-scope agent detects a sub-problem warranting its own autonomy envelope, it writes `extract/{name}.md` (partial LOOP.md slice, trigger, residual scope). Launcher spawns a parallel loop-scope agent for the sub-loop; parent LOOP.md gains `composes-with:` ref when child ships.", "warrant": "Sub-protocols must be declared as named slots before filling; extraction is always a slot-refactor.", "warrant_hash": "sha256:db00a14b4ac5fb8b79a0b7c50bf97731", "verdict": "ADVANCE", "confidence": 0.75, "status": "advance", "updated_at": "2026-07-24T23:34:08.124626+00:00"}
{"idea_id_local": "I-005-DIVERSELOOP", "cluster_id": null, "cycle_id": "cycle-001", "subagent_id": "B-002", "persona": "dreamer", "seed": "s2", "idea_title": "Loop persona × domain-seed diversification matrix", "idea_text": "α-wave generates LOOP.md drafts for one domain, diversified across loop-personas (hostile, divergent, conservative) × domain-seeds (oblique reframe). β stress-tests each; γ synthesizes the canonical LOOP.md from survivors.", "warrant": "Each persona carries a hard structural constraint (hostile: kill-switch per step; divergent: sub-loop escape hatch per step).", "warrant_hash": "sha256:448daf9a0d59c1d1ed8e74c099ea0f7c", "verdict": null, "confidence": null, "status": "deferred", "updated_at": "2026-07-24T23:34:08.124626+00:00"}
{"idea_id_local": "I-001-DEPTH", "cluster_id": "I-001-S2", "cycle_id": "cycle-001", "subagent_id": "B-003", "persona": "skeptic", "seed": "s1", "idea_title": "Extraction-depth budget prevents infinite recursive loop extraction", "idea_text": "", "warrant": "Bounded recursion is textbook; making it a header field mirrors cd-review §0.5.3's hard \"no human\" rule.", "warrant_hash": "sha256:9ab8313382dc35f02f80e4fd3ad2f145", "verdict": "ADVANCE", "confidence": 0.75, "status": "advance", "updated_at": "2026-07-24T23:34:08.124626+00:00"}
{"idea_id_local": "I-002-CANARY", "cluster_id": "I-001-S4", "cycle_id": "cycle-001", "subagent_id": "B-003", "persona": "skeptic", "seed": "s1", "idea_title": "Sealed canary-run gate prevents hidden HITL dependence", "idea_text": "", "warrant": "cd-review §0.5.3 already enforces \"no human\" + crash-safe `day-status.json`; canary is the natural verification counterpart.", "warrant_hash": "sha256:9cbc57c2e5904de1edde5ed677068f90", "verdict": "ADVANCE", "confidence": 0.5, "status": "advance", "updated_at": "2026-07-24T23:34:08.124626+00:00"}
{"idea_id_local": "I-003-DELTA", "cluster_id": "I-001-S3", "cycle_id": "cycle-001", "subagent_id": "B-003", "persona": "skeptic", "seed": "s1", "idea_title": "Baseline delta-test prevents degenerate compositions", "idea_text": "", "warrant": "Baseline comparison is standard ML benchmarking; \"neither parent alone\" is the literal definition of compositionality.", "warrant_hash": "sha256:ec7448c1e08d2649a98121febd9e6803", "verdict": "ADVANCE", "confidence": 0.72, "status": "advance", "updated_at": "2026-07-24T23:34:08.124626+00:00"}
